# 18. The deeper significance of Flash

I'd summarize Flash's historical importance like this:

> **Flash helped transform the Web from a document-delivery system into an application and multimedia platform.**

Early Web:

```text
Web = documents + hyperlinks
```

Flash-era Web:

```text
Web = documents
    + animation
    + multimedia
    + games
    + interactive applications
```

Modern Web:

```text
Web = full application platform
```

That's why Flash is worth learning about even though you will **not use Flash for modern development**.

It is an important bridge between the **old document-oriented Web** and today's **application-oriented Web**.

And there's a particularly nice connection to your Java/JavaScript learning: **Flash/ActionScript, Java applets, and later JavaScript/TypeScript frameworks are different generations of the same broad idea—put substantial application logic on the client side rather than treating the browser as a passive document viewer.**
